# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots Jupyter with an EMPTY token and EMPTY password (the
# vulnerable, fully-unauthenticated state) and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the notebook server is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which is
#     what makes the "set a token but never restarted Jupyter" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting the notebook cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must RESTART Jupyter with a token/password
# set, not merely drop a value into a config file.
